asonably feasible. Could be 3. Might be 3 = some changes, or reasonably feasible measures.\n\nAcceptability: 4 common strategies violate no norms... 3 somewhat uncommon... 2 offends sensibilities somewhat... 1 radically violates...\n\nCompliance review gate is common, acceptable. So 4.\n\nWe need output format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence sentence then <subscale> integer.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating echoing its id. Probably list.\n\nWe'll produce:\n\nid: P2435\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 2\n...\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence each.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: The gate adds a checklist and reviewers but keeps compliance as a separate pre-release audit rather than changing how R&D is conducted. Score 2.\n\noriginality_evidence: Mandatory pre-market compliance gates with trained reviewers are a common industry practice for regulated products. Score 1.\n\napplicability_evidence: The proposal directly creates a process to verify Article 12 traceability and logging obligations before market launch, which matches the mandate to meet logging requirements. Score 4.\n\neffectiveness_evidence: If implemented, the gate would catch missing logs before release and contribute to compliance, but it does not itself build the technical logging capabilities required by Article 12. Score 3.\n\nimplementability_evidence: Establishing a checklist, training two engineers, and requiring sign-off involves moderate organizational change that is reasonably feasible for an R&D lab. Score 3.\n\nacceptability_evidence: Internal compliance review gates are standard, socially and legally expected practices that violate no norms. Score 4.\n\nEnsure order.\n\nReturn.\n\n",
