cle 12.\n\napplicability (1-4): degree to which idea clearly applies to stated problem.\nIt solves implied problem related? Do X to get Y... Publishing papers is not directly solving logging mandate. It may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates. Could be applicability 2: may have some benefit within special situation and somehow relates. Or applicability 3 solves implied problem related. The stated problem is how to meet logging mandate and/or adapt R&D accordingly. Publication series is about adapting R&D perspective? Hmm.\n\nI think applicability = 2 or 3. It maps regulatory fields onto reproducibility criteria, which is related to documentation mandates but not directly implementing logs. Probably \"may have some benefit within a special situation and somehow relates\". So applicability 2.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4): degree to which idea preserves/modifies paradigm.\nParadigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches.\nParadigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\nSlightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice\nParadigm preserving: standard compliance\n\nPublication series positions lab at intersection of regulatory science and methodological rigour... That is changing relationship? Might be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (publications) but still treats compliance as logging practice? Hmm it reframes compliance as evidence quality. Could be paradigm stretching (changes that relationship). Maybe 3.\n\nOriginality (1-4): not expressed before AND ingenious... unusual interesting... common mundane.\nPublication series comparing EU AI Act documentation to reproducibility standards. Is that unusual? Probably interesting but not rare? Might be originality 3 = unusual, interesting; shows some imaginati